  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q001</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Which set of elements constitutes a complete screening liver ultrasound report?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Every field carries decision weight; an impression without adequacy, US category, and findings cannot be acted on or audited.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Impression only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Lesion size and AFP only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Indication, visualization adequacy (VIS-A/B/C), US category (US-1/2/3), parenchymal findings, focal lesions with size and location, AFP if available, impression and recommended next step]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Operator name and date only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q002</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The 'indication' field on a screening report matters because it:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The indication primarily determines surveillance eligibility and clinical context, a cirrhotic patient and a non-cirrhotic HBV carrier qualify under different criteria. Once enrolled, the basic ultrasound recall thresholds applied are generally the same; the indication anchors interpretation rather than changing the recall algorithm itself.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Duplicates the impression]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Records why this patient is in surveillance, which determines whether the patient is correctly eligible for the program]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Is required for billing only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Describes the machine settings]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q003</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>A report impression should be written so that:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The impression is the actionable summary; burying the recommendation in the findings causes missed follow-up.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It avoids any recommendation]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[A referring clinician can act on it without reading the full findings section]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Only a radiologist could interpret it]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[It restates every measurement]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q004</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Recording the date the next screen is due on a negative report primarily:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Surveillance fails at the interval far more often than at the scan; the next-due date is the operational fix.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Satisfies audit requirements only]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Converts a negative result into a scheduled action, which is what sustains interval adherence]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Replaces the recall algorithm]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Is optional in most programs]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q005</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Which impression is most appropriate for a complete study showing a coarse nodular liver, splenomegaly, and no focal lesion?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The impression should state the visualization score, the US category, the parenchymal finding, the absence of focal disease, and the next action. A truly complete, unremarkable study like this one would typically be US-1/VIS-A.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Normal liver ultrasound]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Limited study, repeat]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Abnormal liver, refer urgently]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Adequate study (VIS-A). US-1. Cirrhotic morphology with splenomegaly. No focal lesion identified. Continue 6-month surveillance; next due [date]]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
    <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q007</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Which phrase in a report is most likely to cause downstream harm?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>'No evidence of malignancy' overstates what a screening ultrasound can establish and invites false reassurance.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Adequate visualization]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[No focal lesion seen in the visualized liver]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Technically limited study]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[No evidence of malignancy]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
    <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q009</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Severe steatosis with deep attenuation should be reflected in the report because it:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The negative predictive value of the study is lower, and the reader needs to know that.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Is a benign incidental finding requiring no mention]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Indicates cirrhosis]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Reduces sensitivity for focal lesions, which changes how a negative result should be interpreted]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Requires immediate referral]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q010</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>A 46-year-old with HBV cirrhosis. Adequate study. A 0.7 cm hypoechoic nodule in segment VI, new since the last scan. AFP 6 ng/mL. The appropriate recommendation is:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Sub-centimetre nodules enter short-interval follow-up; both size and AFP are below recall thresholds.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Biopsy]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Return to routine 6-month surveillance with no change]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Repeat ultrasound in 3-6 months to assess for growth]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Multiphase CT or MRI now]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>Q011</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>A 52-year-old with cirrhosis. Adequate study. A 2.1 cm heterogeneous lesion with a thin halo in segment VIII. AFP 11 ng/mL. The appropriate recommendation is:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>A lesion of 1 cm or greater triggers diagnostic imaging regardless of AFP; a normal AFP does not downgrade it.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.0000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Reassure, as AFP is normal]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Refer for multiphase contrast-enhanced CT or MRI]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[Repeat ultrasound in 3 months]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
